<task id="032" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Tool: spaarke_get_matter_summary (cached, else start a run)</title>
    <phase>2 Long-running work, AI, widgets, task writes</phase>
    <gate>r1 gate RELEASED 2026-11-25 (joint mcp-r1/mcp-r2 determination under the owner's delegation; see notes/decisions.md D-r1-gate). Before starting, merge origin/master into this branch (merge, never rebase). Do not edit r1's ISS-010 files (DecisionCommitService, Actions/DecisionActionExecutors, RecordCreationService, CallerWriteAuthorization, CallerRecordAccessProbe, CallerMetadataReadMemo, AssignTaskNotifier, the email-bell job handler) or the Decision wizard heading files (DecisionWizard/steps/FoundStep.tsx, Worklist/IssueLine.tsx, composeIssueLine.ts) without messaging mcp-r1 first.</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New BFF surface that may start an AI run; second user of the long-running pattern</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Composes existing pieces (012's topic and column, TopicRegistryTtlLookup, 030's run start/status) with an explicit escalation if they do not fit</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>I</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/MatterSummary/** and its ledger partial; runs after 030 (reuses its run path)</parallel-reason>
    <deps>012, 020, 030</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, ai, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add the read-only-first MCP tool spaarke_get_matter_summary: read the matter-summary topic result for a matter as the caller (the sprk_matter column task 012 added, with its date) and, if it is fresh under the sprk_aitopicregistry TTL (TopicRegistryTtlLookup), return it; if missing or expired, start a matter-summary run through the same run path task 030 uses and return McpLongRunning.Started, so spaarke_get_playbook_run returns the fresh summary. No new summary store.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in the Insights topic registry, work-product persistence and MCP tool handlers.</role>
  <goal>A cached summary returns in ≤ 3 s and matches the matter form's insight card; an expired one starts exactly one run and the status tool returns the fresh summary; a caller who cannot read the matter gets a uniform not-found.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-10, FR-14; owner: complete the matter-summary topic (task 012: new sprk_matter column + registry row; WorkProductRecordPersister writes it). Services/Ai/Insights/TopicRegistryTtlLookup.cs (TryGetTtlForPlaybookIdAsync :124, ...ByName :170); InsightsPlaybookExecutionCache.GetOrExecuteAsync (:130) runs synchronously, so it cannot be the start path under the 30 s rule. Run start/status: task 030 (PlaybookOrchestrationService + durable record).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/MatterSummary/GetMatterSummaryTool.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Mcp.MatterSummary.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/MatterSummary/GetMatterSummaryToolTests.cs (fresh → cached result; expired/missing → Started; matter unreadable → not-found)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Insights/TopicRegistryTtlLookup.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/WorkProductRecordPersister.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Playbooks/RunPlaybookTool.cs (task 030)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/012-matter-summary-topic.md (column name, playbook id, TTL)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="012" status="pending">matter-summary column and registry row on dev</dependency>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">McpLongRunning</dependency>
      <dependency task="030" status="pending">Run start/status path</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">r1 gate RELEASED 2026-11-25 (joint mcp-r1/mcp-r2 determination under the owner's delegation; see notes/decisions.md D-r1-gate). Before starting, merge origin/master into this branch (merge, never rebase). Do not edit r1's ISS-010 files (DecisionCommitService, Actions/DecisionActionExecutors, RecordCreationService, CallerWriteAuthorization, CallerRecordAccessProbe, CallerMetadataReadMemo, AssignTaskNotifier, the email-bell job handler) or the Decision wizard heading files (DecisionWizard/steps/FoundStep.tsx, Worklist/IssueLine.tsx, composeIssueLine.ts) without messaging mcp-r1 first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Read the matter column as the caller (IDataverseUserClient, user OBO) so Dataverse enforces read access; unreadable and missing matters return the same not-found. No app-only read.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No new store, table, cache or background worker (FR-10, ADR-052): freshness = column timestamp vs the registry TTL; the start path is 030's run start (with the matter as subject), so the persister writes the column on completion. If 030's path cannot target the matter-summary Binding, STOP and escalate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">readOnlyHint false (it can start a run), destructiveHint false, idempotentHint true; a second call while a run for the same matter is in flight returns that run's id, not a new run. Description says "AI summary of one matter"; not finance, not health.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Model-visible: summary text ≤ 2,000 chars and its generated date; no secured matter fields. Logs: tool name, latency, outcome (cached|started|not-found), correlation id.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source: spec.md 'Placement &amp; New Components'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, 55 MB total triggers architecture review, 60 MB is a hard stop. No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master. CS0618 is a build error: migrate, never suppress.</constraint>
  </constraints>

