  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm the r1 gate and 012, 020, 030; read notes/012 and how the insight card reads the column.</step>
    <step order="2">Write the tool (fresh → return; else start via 030's path; in-flight → same run id) and ledger row.</step>
    <step order="3">Write the tests; run MCP suites, ArchTests and conformance; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="4">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="5">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the insight card reads the summary from somewhere other than the persisted column (so "matches the card" cannot hold), STOP and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>If detecting an in-flight run for the matter needs a new store, STOP and escalate with the §11 answers.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md row "Matter AI summary" (Insights cache + TopicRegistryTtlLookup); task 012's column/registry row; task 030's run tools.</existing>
    <extension>Everything is reused; the tool composes them.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Copilot users cannot get a matter's AI summary (FR-10 fails).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build; dotnet test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/MatterSummary/GetMatterSummaryTool.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/MatterSummary/GetMatterSummaryToolTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A column value newer than the TTL returns { summary, generatedOn } without starting a run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A missing or expired value returns { runId, status, consoleLink } and starts exactly one run; a second call while it runs returns the same runId.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an unreadable and a non-existent matter return byte-identical not-found results; no caller context returns UserContextRequired.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ArchTests and conformance pass; publish-size delta recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-10, FR-14. Live ≤ 3 s check runs in 042.</notes>

